'' 'x = type<T>( y )' over the same type is a COPY of y, not a field list. Measured:
'' fbc emits '__builtin_memcpy( &X$0, &Y$0, 4 )' for it, and the same for the three
'' parenthesised spellings structs/anon-param writes beside it to say they are one
'' thing. The field-list path could not take it -- T's first field is a LONG and the
'' argument is a T -- so the whole assignment declined.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/typelit-copy.bas
